@prefix gmeow:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv:   <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix prov:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix np:       <http://www.nanopub.org/nschema#> .
@prefix crminf:   <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMinf/> .
@prefix wikibase: <http://wikiba.se/ontology#> .
@prefix wd:       <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .
@prefix schema:   <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix oa:       <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix dul:      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#> .
@prefix iao:      <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix iptc:     <http://iptc.org/std/NewsML-G2/> .
@prefix bbc:      <http://www.bbc.co.uk/ontologies/news/> .

# Term equivalences for the standpoint / contested-claims facility (standpoint facility) — GMEOW
# authoring source. Compiled to mappings/gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv by
# `gmeow compile-mappings`. All alignments are BY REFERENCE (Principle 5); GMEOW
# never imports an external axiom. The facility realises the formal Standpoint
# Logic line (Gómez Álvarez & Rudolph), which validates and grounds GMEOW's design.
# See docs/standpoints.md and docs/standpoint-mapping.md.

gmeow:mapsetStandpoint a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/standpoint" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    # Authored multi-line for readability; the compiler collapses whitespace so the
    # SSSOM TSV header carries it on a single line (compile-check verifies no drift).
    gmeow:setComment """Standpoint / contested-claims alignments (standpoint facility).
        FORMAL GROUNDING: gmeow:accordingTo is the axiom-level standpoint label of Standpoint Logic (Gómez Álvarez & Rudolph — Standpoint EL, IJCAI 2023; Standpoint-OWL 2, arXiv:2305.00559; Monodic-S5 over OWL 2 DL, KR 2025); gmeow:standpointModality unequivocal/conceivable are the box/diamond operators; gmeow:sharpens is the standpoint subset/precisification relation; gmeow:universalStandpoint is the universal standpoint *.
        The Standpoint-OWL 2 standpointLabel encoding is GENERATED as a lossless projection (queries/projections/standpoint-owl2.rq) — Box=□ unequivocal, Diamond=◊ conceivable, name=* universal — so an off-the-shelf standpoint reasoner (cl-tud/standpoint-owl2 → an off-the-shelf OWL 2 DL reasoner) can run per-/cross-standpoint consistency over GMEOW's full multi-perspective graph.
        ORTHOGONALITY: gmeow:accordingTo (whose frame) is distinct from prov:wasAttributedTo (which source recorded it — relatedMatch only, never closeMatch) and gmeow:confidence (how sure we are).
        NANOPUBLICATIONS: gmeow:StatementMetadata reuses the nanopublication assertion/provenance split and adds the temporal standpoint axis.
        TRANSCENDENCE: GMEOW supersets the event-centric Attributions model (arXiv:2503.03563) — its stated limitations of static viewpoints (no time) and neutral-stance ambiguity are met by gmeow:StandpointTenure (standpoint-time) and the three orthogonal axes; GMEOW is View-Preserving (no forced propagation), so the aggregate/constituent representation paradox cannot arise.
        CRMinf PARITY: GMEOW is at least as expressive as the CIDOC-CRM Argumentation model — the reified statement is an I4 Proposition Set, a StandpointTenure is a (temporal) I2 Belief, the standpoint is the actor of an I1 Argumentation, and gmeow:standpointModality spans the J5-holds-to-be belief value (true/probable/possible/false), so a denial is first-class, not just an absence. It is GENERATED as a lossless projection (queries/projections/standpoint-crminf.rq).
        FACTORED MODALITY: claim modality is now the six orthogonal axes (gmeow:Polarity / ModalForce / CredenceLevel / AssertoricForce / TruthDirectedness / SupportStatus), of which the legacy five-value gmeow:standpointModality is the lossless projection — so GMEOW remains at least as expressive as CRMinf (the belief value rides gmeow:Polarity + gmeow:ModalForce + gmeow:CredenceLevel) while ALSO subsuming the Belnap four-valued support status (gmeow:SupportStatus, aligned by prose to logic:InformationState) and the Frankfurt bullshit stance (gmeow:TruthDirectedness indifferent) that CRMinf's belief value cannot express.
        A standpoint-indexed claim is also a PROV-O entity attributed to its standpoint agent, a W3C Web Annotation (body/target/creator), and a DOLCE+DnS Situation read from the standpoint's Description — projected, respectively, by standpoint-prov.rq and standpoint-oa.rq.
        It relates conceptually (no clean GMEOW-term row, or no stable RDF namespace, to align) to: CKR contexts (GMEOW factors time/place into its own modules, keeping only the perspective axis here); MVP-OWL multi-viewpoint classes; ClaiMaker source-anchored claims; the NdFluents/4dFluents family of contextualization mechanisms (GMEOW's RDF-1.2 reification is the benchmarked-best such mechanism); the Argument Interchange Format (AIF: I-nodes for the claims, CA-nodes for the conflicts between coexisting standpoints); and SPAR CiTO citation functions (cito:disputes/supports/refutes) — which GMEOW realises structurally as coexisting, modality-valued claims rather than as inter-entity edges.""" ;
    gmeow:setTrailer "# REFUSED (Principle 9 — no single slot to win): standpoint-indexed claims are co-equal; GMEOW has no preferred/primary claim.\n# gmeow:accordingTo  ✗ REFUSED  wikibase:rank / wikibase:PreferredRank — a preferred rank re-creates the single winner that IS the object of the edit war. GMEOW keeps Wikidata references/qualifiers as relatedMatch targets but never adopts rank." .

# Source attribution — distinct from the standpoint frame (a neutral source can
# record a partisan claim), so a loose relatedMatch, never closeMatch.
gmeow:accordingTo skos:relatedMatch prov:wasAttributedTo {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "standpoint (whose frame the claim holds in) is distinct from source attribution (which agent recorded it); only a loose relatedMatch"
|} .

# Nanopublications — GMEOW's reified statement reuses the assertion/provenance
# split and adds the standpoint + temporal axes.
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch np:Nanopublication {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "a reified statement-with-provenance is a nanopublication minus the persistent identifier; GMEOW adds the standpoint axis and the four clocks"
|} .

# CRMinf — the CIDOC-CRM Argumentation/belief model: who holds which proposition
# true, over what time. Its I2 Belief is itself temporal, mirroring GMEOW's
# standpoint-time (the StandpointTenure). The reified statement IS a proposition
# set held as a belief.
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch crminf:I4_Proposition_Set {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the reified base triple is the proposition set a belief is about (CRMinf J4 that)"
|} .

gmeow:StandpointTenure skos:relatedMatch crminf:I2_Belief {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint holding a position over an interval is a temporal belief (CRMinf I2 Belief is a subclass of E2 Temporal Entity — the same standpoint-time)"
|} .

# Wikidata's reified statement model — keep its statement node + the supported-by
# qualifier as alignment targets; the rank family is REFUSED (see the trailer).
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch wikibase:Statement {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "GMEOW's reifier is Wikidata's statement node — but with no rank (Principle 9)"
|} .

gmeow:accordingTo skos:relatedMatch wd:P3680 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "Wikidata 'statement supported by' (P3680) names who backs a statement — GMEOW's standpoint frame; its inverse 'statement disputed by' (P1310) is, in GMEOW, simply another coexisting standpoint-indexed claim"
|} .

# schema.org — a standpoint-indexed claim is the thing a schema:Claim names (and a
# schema:ClaimReview's verdict is just one standpoint's claim, never a winner).
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch schema:Claim {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a reified, standpoint-indexed claim corresponds to schema:Claim; GMEOW refuses the single-verdict false-credibility of ClaimReview"
|} .

# The belief-value axis — at least as expressive as CRMinf: J5 holds to be assigns
# a proposition set its belief value (true/false/probable/possible), exactly the
# gmeow:standpointModality value space (unequivocal/refuted/probable/conceivable).
gmeow:standpointModality skos:relatedMatch crminf:J5_holds_to_be {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "the standpoint's belief value over the proposition — GMEOW's modality (unequivocal/probable/conceivable/refuted) spans CRMinf's true/probable/possible/false"
|} .

# PROV-O — a standpoint-indexed claim is a provenance entity attributed to its
# standpoint agent (projected as a qualified attribution, queries/.../standpoint-prov.rq).
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch prov:Entity {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a reified claim is a prov:Entity attributed (prov:qualifiedAttribution) to its standpoint agent"
|} .

gmeow:Standpoint skos:relatedMatch prov:Agent {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint is often (not always) a prov:Agent — the bearer of an attribution; relatedMatch because a frame need not be an actor"
|} .

# W3C Web Annotation — a reified, attributed assertion is an annotation: the quoted
# triple is the body, its subject the target, the standpoint the creator.
gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch oa:Annotation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint-indexed claim corresponds to an oa:Annotation (body = the quoted triple, target = its subject, creator = the standpoint)"
|} .

# DOLCE+DnS (Descriptions & Situations) — a standpoint is a description (a
# conceptualization/perspective); the claim it frames is the situation it satisfies.
gmeow:Standpoint skos:relatedMatch dul:Description {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint is a DnS Description — a conceptualization/perspective from which states of affairs are read"
|} .

gmeow:StatementMetadata skos:relatedMatch dul:Situation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.35 ;
    gmeow:comment "the standpoint-indexed claim is the DnS Situation that satisfies the standpoint's Description"
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# StandpointTenure observation design — StandpointClaim as Observation specialization (deepenings + new)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

# IAO (Information Artifact Ontology) — a StandpointClaim is an assertion.
gmeow:StandpointClaim skos:closeMatch iao:assertion {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint claim is an assertion in the IAO sense — an information content entity that bears a proposition"
|} .

gmeow:observedFeature skos:relatedMatch iao:information_content_entity {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the proposition/fact being claimed (the observedFeature of a StandpointClaim) is the information content entity the assertion is about"
|} .

# CRMinf deepening — StandpointClaim as Inference_Making; claimModality as J5.
gmeow:StandpointClaim skos:closeMatch crminf:I5_Inference_Making {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint claim is an inference-making act concluding a belief (CRMinf I5)"
|} .

gmeow:claimModality skos:closeMatch crminf:J5_holds_to_be {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "the observationResult of a StandpointClaim is the belief value (CRMinf J5)"
|} .

# IPTC / BBC News Ontology — media-standpoint alignments.
gmeow:Standpoint skos:relatedMatch iptc:Assertor {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "when the vantage is a news organization, it acts as an IPTC Assertor"
|} .

gmeow:Event skos:relatedMatch bbc:NewsEvent {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.45 ;
    gmeow:comment "a standpoint-claim about an event projects to a BBC NewsEvent; the projection is conditional on the observedFeature being an Event"
|} .

# W3C Web Annotation deepening — StandpointClaim as Annotation.
gmeow:StandpointClaim skos:relatedMatch oa:Annotation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "a StandpointClaim projects to an OA Annotation via a directional lowering (body is the claim, target is the observedFeature); not interchangeable, so relatedMatch"
|} .

gmeow:vantage skos:relatedMatch oa:annotatedBy {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the vantage of a StandpointClaim is the annotator in OA terms"
|} .

gmeow:observedFeature skos:relatedMatch oa:hasTarget {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "the observedFeature of a StandpointClaim is the target of the OA Annotation"
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# the design — bullshit modality (Frankfurt) as a fifth StandpointModality value.
# CRMinf I6_Belief_Value spans true/probable/possible/false; GMEOW adds bullshit.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

gmeow:bullshit skos:relatedMatch crminf:I6_Belief_Value {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the bullshit modality (indifference to truth) extends CRMinf's belief value space — it is neither true nor false, but a distinct stance toward correspondence"
|} .

# Factored claim-modality axes — per-axis CRMinf alignments. The legacy
# gmeow:standpointModality (eqStandpoint008) stays the lossless projection these
# axes decompose; each axis is aligned to the CRMinf belief-value surface it
# refines, keeping the "at least as expressive as CRMinf" invariant.

gmeow:standpointPolarity skos:relatedMatch crminf:J5_holds_to_be {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "the affirm/deny/suspend polarity axis refines CRMinf's J5 holds-to-be — gmeow:polarityDeny is the canonical carrier of the J5 'false' belief value (the legacy gmeow:refuted projection), frame-relative, never global-false (Principle 9)"
|} .

gmeow:standpointModalForce skos:relatedMatch crminf:I6_Belief_Value {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the alethic modal-force axis (Standpoint-Logic box/diamond — necessary/actual/possible/counterfactual) refines the CRMinf belief-value space, carrying the true/possible distinction CRMinf's J5 collapses"
|} .

gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness skos:relatedMatch crminf:I6_Belief_Value {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the truth-directedness axis (truth-aimed/indifferent/strategic) extends CRMinf's belief-value space — gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt bullshit) is a stance toward correspondence CRMinf's J5 cannot express; this is the axis-level successor to eqStandpoint023 (gmeow:bullshit)"
|} .

gmeow:standpointSupportStatus skos:relatedMatch crminf:I6_Belief_Value {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-standpoint.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the Belnap evidential-support axis (supported/opposed/both/neither) extends CRMinf's belief-value space with proof/counterproof status, including the witnessed glut (gmeow:supportBoth) CRMinf cannot carry; the domain twin of logic:InformationState (now merged) — that internal cross-slice bridge stays prose (skos:scopeNote on each value) + a logic:formalizes back-reference from the logic slice, kept out of this external-vocabulary SSSOM by design"
|} .
